igm Daleks debuting things I don't  want to say fall apart but they just get  a little ridiculous and I mean doctor  who can be ridiculous and sometimes it  can be very arbitrary what does or  doesn't like feel legitimate but the  Spitfires flying into space feels like a  stretch the the Android that had been  passed off as the human inventor of the  Ironsides who apparently didn't even  know he was a robot he's a bomb okay  that's totally something the Daleks  would do cool  he deactivates his bomb miss by feeling  lots of fields shuts down the bomb so  he's not a bomb now because he felt  I'm not gonna say that I can't go to  some degree with the idea that him  tapping into his humanity would somehow  break whatever restraints the Daleks had  to keep him alive and made sure he did  what they wanted him to do and you know  properly freed him but having it  actually deactivate a bomb that I have a  hard time imagining the Daleks wouldn't  have rigged up to be completely separate  from whatever was going on with his  brain and fit in fake as far as they  were concerned fake emotions and it just  it just feels like a bit of a stretch I  also strongly suspect that it's here not  because this story needs it but to  introduce the idea of an artificial  human being still being validly human  because that's gonna come up again later  in later in the season so I strongly  suspect that's why it's here in the  first place and I can't prove this or if  there is evidence of it I haven't found  it cuz I don't really do research but my  suspicion is that the inclusion of that  angle was a directive from Moffat  because he saw it as an opportunity to  set up some stuff that he was gonna do  later on in the series or at least set  up some of these concepts and lay some  of the ground work because within the  confines of this story we we don't need  it it yeah it just doesn't it doesn't  quite work it doesn't quite fit and it's  a little it's a bit cheesy er than what  had come up - well I mean it's about as  cheesy as the spitfires I suppose but it  really did feel like wow the Daleks are  winning you know the doctors doing his  best but he's on the backfoot the doctor  the Daleks really have him now and now  they're Spitfires and a bomb robot with  fields so he's okay now it's a bit of a  it's a bit of a jarring shift tonally in  terms  what the sort of level of reality is for  this episode and doctor who can get away  with adjusting the woeful suspension of  disbelief and sort of the reality of the  story from episode to episode but when  you have it shift like that within the  same episode that that doesn't work so  well and it's a shame because like I  said I actually think there's a lot of  good in this episode I think it's an  underrated episode truth be told but I  also recognize the problems with it and  that it ends with a soft very soft hit  like the the shutting down of that of  that bomb is not the cathartic climax  that this thing needs because I mean we  were dealing with the Daleks and we end  with aging human robot is gonna go look  for the town and the girl from his  memories to see if they're real I mean  yay but it just it it's not the climax  and the feel and the conclusion to a  Dalek story if that makes sense but  victory of the Daleks you seen it lately  what do you think about it whatever your  thoughts are drop something down the  comments and let's talk about it there's  a whole bunch of stuff to do as well  because you can like you can subscribe  you can support me on patreon which  helps me cover the bills and and ideally  one of these days get to legitimately  start doing bigger and better projects  and plus there's other stuff down below  as well link to the book I've published  oh the patreon also gets you on to my  author diary because I'm working on  another book of work of fiction this  time and author Diaries are going up on  the patreon page and yeah I plugged that  enough but there's other links besides  that socials Instagram Twitter etc etc  click on stuff it'll take you places  check it out or don't I'm not gonna tell  you what to do because at the end of the  day you're the council  just run in the meetings and until next  time this council is adjourned  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

